1
00:00:07,350 --> 00:00:11,798
Here are the three jobs and the three candidates from the first episode,

2
00:00:11,798 --> 00:00:14,332
each with the same ranked list as before.

3
00:00:14,332 --> 00:00:20,006
The first name under a header is the favourite, and the last name is the least wanted.

4
00:00:20,183 --> 00:00:22,595
What should a good matching do for them?

5
00:00:22,595 --> 00:00:28,813
We could give as many of them as possible their first choice, or as few as possible their last choice.

6
00:00:28,813 --> 00:00:35,017
Or we could add up how far down its list everybody lands, and make that total small.

7
00:00:35,183 --> 00:00:41,405
But all of these are scores handed down from above, and jobs and candidates are free to act on their own.

8
00:00:41,405 --> 00:00:45,015
So let us look at one matching through their eyes.

9
00:00:46,183 --> 00:00:53,089
Take this matching, where Approximation has Christine, Basis has Bridget, and Control has Anita.

10
00:00:53,089 --> 00:00:58,387
Start with Approximation, which sits at the bottom of its own list with Christine,

11
00:00:58,387 --> 00:01:00,455
so it would rather have Bridget.

12
00:01:00,616 --> 00:01:04,756
But wanting is not enough, because Bridget has to want it too.

13
00:01:04,756 --> 00:01:11,054
Bridget has Basis, the second name on her list, and the first name on her list is Approximation.

14
00:01:11,054 --> 00:01:15,181
So Approximation and Bridget would both rather have each other,

15
00:01:15,181 --> 00:01:18,980
and they can simply walk away from this matching together.

16
00:01:19,150 --> 00:01:21,610
And look what that does to the others.

17
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:25,731
Approximation drops Christine, who is suddenly without a job,

18
00:01:25,731 --> 00:01:29,988
and Bridget leaves Basis, which suddenly has an empty position.

19
00:01:29,988 --> 00:01:36,758
A pair like this is called a rogue couple, and a matching that contains one is called unstable.

20
00:01:36,916 --> 00:01:39,280
Is that the only rogue couple here?

21
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:43,308
Approximation also ranks Anita above Christine, and Anita,

22
00:01:43,308 --> 00:01:48,308
who has Control at the bottom of her list, ranks Approximation above it.

23
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:56,336
So Approximation and Anita are a second rogue couple, and one is already enough to make a matching unstable.

24
00:01:58,516 --> 00:02:05,684
Now try a different matching, where Approximation has Bridget, Basis has Anita, and Control has Christine.

25
00:02:05,684 --> 00:02:09,718
To hunt for a rogue couple we can go through the jobs one at a time.

26
00:02:09,718 --> 00:02:16,610
A job only prefers the names above its partner, so those are the only candidates we need to ask.

27
00:02:16,783 --> 00:02:20,531
Approximation has Bridget and would rather have Anita.

28
00:02:20,531 --> 00:02:25,761
But Anita has Basis, the very first name on her list, so she will not move.

29
00:02:25,761 --> 00:02:30,813
That is why Approximation and Anita are no rogue couple here.

30
00:02:30,983 --> 00:02:36,093
Basis has Anita and would rather have Bridget, but Bridget has Approximation,

31
00:02:36,093 --> 00:02:39,079
which is first on her list, so she stays too.

32
00:02:39,079 --> 00:02:46,107
Control would rather have Anita or Bridget, and we have just seen that each of them holds her first choice.

33
00:02:46,283 --> 00:02:49,957
So every job has been checked and no rogue couple turned up,

34
00:02:49,957 --> 00:02:53,203
and a matching with no rogue couple is called stable.

35
00:02:53,203 --> 00:02:58,125
Notice that Control and Christine are both stuck with the last name on their lists.

36
00:02:58,125 --> 00:03:05,529
So stable does not mean everyone is happy, only that nobody can find a partner who wants to leave with them.

37
00:03:05,683 --> 00:03:10,691
This is not the matching that propose and reject gave us in the first episode.

38
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:16,655
That one paired Approximation with Anita, Basis with Bridget, and Control with Christine.

39
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:20,186
There, only Control has names above its partner,

40
00:03:20,186 --> 00:03:25,335
and Anita and Bridget each rank Control last, so it is stable as well.

41
00:03:25,516 --> 00:03:29,338
So one set of lists can have more than one stable matching.

42
00:03:29,338 --> 00:03:32,642
But we found both of them by luck and by checking.

43
00:03:32,642 --> 00:03:36,642
Does every set of lists have a stable matching at all?

